[{"id":"D3-0001","d":3,"o":"3.1","x":"easy","q":"During an outage of the central authentication service, a badge-controlled server room falls back to denying all entry until service is restored. Which secure design principle does this illustrate?","c":["Fail securely","Least privilege","Separation of duties","Defense in depth"],"k":""},{"id":"D3-0002","d":3,"o":"3.6","x":"hard","q":"A vendor distributes firmware updates through public mirrors and must let devices confirm that each image is authentic and unmodified before installation. Which mechanism BEST meets this requirement?","c":["A digital signature over each firmware image","A SHA-256 hash published beside each image","An HMAC computed with a shared device key","TLS encryption for every download session"],"k":""},{"id":"D3-0003","d":3,"o":"3.2","x":"easy","q":"A military system must prevent users from reading documents classified above their clearance level. Which security model directly enforces this 'no read up' rule?","c":["Bell-LaPadula","Biba","Clark-Wilson","Brewer-Nash"],"k":""},{"id":"D3-0004","d":3,"o":"3.5","x":"medium","q":"A privileged installer checks a file's permissions, and an attacker swaps the file for a symbolic link in the instant between that check and the privileged write. Which vulnerability class is being exploited?","c":["A buffer overflow in the installer","An insecure direct object reference","A time-of-check to time-of-use race condition","A privilege escalation via DLL injection"],"k":""},{"id":"D3-0005","d":3,"o":"3.7","x":"hard","q":"Researchers recover an encryption key from a smart card by passively measuring fluctuations in its power consumption during cryptographic operations. Which attack class does this represent?","c":["A chosen-plaintext attack","A side-channel attack","A brute-force attack","A fault-injection attack"],"k":""},{"id":"D3-0006","d":3,"o":"3.9","x":"easy","q":"A data center wants to stop an unauthorized person from slipping through a secure entrance behind an employee's single badge swipe. Which physical control BEST addresses this?","c":["CCTV cameras covering the entrance","Additional badge readers on interior doors","Security awareness posters at the door","A mantrap with interlocking doors"],"k":""},{"id":"D3-0007","d":3,"o":"3.4","x":"medium","q":"A laptop fleet must release its disk encryption keys only when each machine boots with untampered firmware and boot loader. Which hardware capability provides this?","c":["A Trusted Platform Module measuring the boot chain","A hardware security module in the data center","Self-encrypting drives with drive-lock passwords","UEFI passwords protecting the firmware menu"],"k":""}]
